{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "name": "Incident Intake API",
    "description": "REST API for the Incident Intake microservice.\n\nBase URL variable: `base_url` (default: http://localhost:8080)\n\nWorkflow tip: run **Create Incident** first — the test script auto-saves the returned `id` into the `incident_id` collection variable so all subsequent requests are pre-filled.\n\nStatus transitions (feature/MVP):\n  OPEN → IN_PROGRESS | ON_HOLD\n  IN_PROGRESS → RESOLVED | ON_HOLD\n  ON_HOLD → IN_PROGRESS | CLOSED\n  RESOLVED → CLOSED\n\nThe **Chat (Claude)** folder exercises the same flows through natural language against POST /chat, backed by an Anthropic Claude model wired to all five MCP tools (create_incident, get_incident, list_incidents, update_incident_status, get_incident_history). Run its requests in order — each one reuses `conversation_id`, auto-saved by the first chat request's test script, so the model retains context across turns.\n\nThe **MCP Context** folder hits GET /mcp/tools, which lists every registered MCP tool with its name, description, and JSON input schema.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "incident_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Auto-populated by the Create Incident test script"
    },
    {
      "key": "conversation_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Auto-populated by the first Chat request's test script; reused by subsequent chat requests for multi-turn memory"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Incidents",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Incident — CRITICAL",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Response has id', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.id).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('incident_id', body.id);",
                  "    console.log('incident_id set to', body.id);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Status is OPEN', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('OPEN');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Database connection pool exhausted on prod-db-01\",\n  \"severity\": \"CRITICAL\",\n  \"reportedBy\": \"alice@example.com\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents"]
            },
            "description": "Creates a new incident. Returns 201 on creation, 200 if the same externalReferenceId was already submitted (idempotency hit)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create Incident — HIGH (idempotent)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 or 200', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('externalReferenceId echoed back', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().externalReferenceId).to.eql('EXT-REF-001');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Payment service latency spike\",\n  \"severity\": \"HIGH\",\n  \"reportedBy\": \"bob@example.com\",\n  \"externalReferenceId\": \"EXT-REF-001\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents"]
            },
            "description": "Submit the same externalReferenceId twice to verify idempotency — the second call returns HTTP 200 with the existing record."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List All Incidents",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response is array', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents"]
            },
            "description": "Returns all incidents. No filters applied."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Incidents — filter by severity",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('All results are CRITICAL', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.json().forEach(i => pm.expect(i.severity).to.eql('CRITICAL'));",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents?severity=CRITICAL",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "severity", "value": "CRITICAL", "description": "LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL" },
                { "key": "status", "value": "", "disabled": true, "description": "OPEN | IN_PROGRESS | ON_HOLD | RESOLVED | CLOSED" },
                { "key": "reportedBy", "value": "", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Filter by severity. Combine with `status` and `reportedBy` as needed."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Incidents — filter by status ON_HOLD",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('All results are ON_HOLD', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.json().forEach(i => pm.expect(i.status).to.eql('ON_HOLD'));",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents?status=ON_HOLD",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "status", "value": "ON_HOLD", "description": "OPEN | IN_PROGRESS | ON_HOLD | RESOLVED | CLOSED" },
                { "key": "severity", "value": "", "disabled": true, "description": "LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL" },
                { "key": "reportedBy", "value": "", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Filter incidents currently paused (ON_HOLD)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Incident by ID",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('ID matches', () => {",
                  "    const id = pm.collectionVariables.get('incident_id');",
                  "    if (id) pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.eql(id);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/{{incident_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents", "{{incident_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Retrieve a single incident. `incident_id` is auto-set by the Create Incident test script."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Status → IN_PROGRESS",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Status is IN_PROGRESS', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('IN_PROGRESS');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"IN_PROGRESS\",\n  \"changedBy\": \"alice@example.com\",\n  \"notes\": \"Assigned to on-call team, investigating connection pool settings.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/{{incident_id}}/status",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents", "{{incident_id}}", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Valid from OPEN. Moves the incident into active work."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Status → ON_HOLD",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Status is ON_HOLD', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('ON_HOLD');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"ON_HOLD\",\n  \"changedBy\": \"bob@example.com\",\n  \"notes\": \"Waiting for DBA approval before changing pool size.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/{{incident_id}}/status",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents", "{{incident_id}}", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Valid from OPEN or IN_PROGRESS. Pauses work while preserving full context."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Status → RESOLVED",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Status is RESOLVED', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('RESOLVED');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('resolvedAt is set', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().resolvedAt).to.not.be.null;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"RESOLVED\",\n  \"changedBy\": \"alice@example.com\",\n  \"notes\": \"Increased pool size from 10 to 50, restarted app servers. Monitoring for 30 min.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/{{incident_id}}/status",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents", "{{incident_id}}", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Valid from IN_PROGRESS. Sets `resolvedAt` timestamp."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Status → CLOSED",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Status is CLOSED', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('CLOSED');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"CLOSED\",\n  \"changedBy\": \"alice@example.com\",\n  \"notes\": \"Stable for 24 hours. Post-mortem scheduled.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/{{incident_id}}/status",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents", "{{incident_id}}", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Valid from RESOLVED or ON_HOLD. Terminal state — no further transitions allowed."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Status — invalid transition (expect 422)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 422 Unprocessable Entity', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"CLOSED\",\n  \"changedBy\": \"test-user\",\n  \"notes\": \"Trying to skip directly to CLOSED from OPEN\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/{{incident_id}}/status",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents", "{{incident_id}}", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Demonstrates the 422 response returned for illegal state transitions (e.g. OPEN → CLOSED). Run this against a freshly created (OPEN) incident."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Chat (Claude)",
      "description": "Natural-language flows against POST /chat. The assistant is a Claude model wired to all five MCP tools (create_incident, get_incident, list_incidents, update_incident_status, get_incident_history), so each request below drives the same backend logic as the Incidents/Audit REST folders — just phrased as a conversation.\n\nRun requests top to bottom. The first request omits `conversationId` so the server generates one and the test script saves it into `conversation_id`; every later request sends that value back so the model keeps multi-turn context (e.g. remembering which incident was just discussed).\n\nRequires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` to be set on the running server — these calls hit the real Claude API and will 500 without it.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Chat: Create Incident",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response has reply and conversationId', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.reply).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(body.conversationId).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('conversation_id', body.conversationId);",
                  "    console.log('conversation_id set to', body.conversationId);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Create a new CRITICAL incident titled 'Redis cluster failover loop', reported by chat-user@example.com.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/chat",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["chat"]
            },
            "description": "First turn — no conversationId sent, so the server mints a new one. Expect the model to invoke create_incident and confirm creation in its reply."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Chat: List Incidents by Severity",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('conversationId echoed back unchanged', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.conversationId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('conversation_id'));",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Show me every CRITICAL incident currently open.\",\n  \"conversationId\": \"{{conversation_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/chat",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["chat"]
            },
            "description": "Exercises list_incidents with a severity filter. Continues the same conversation started above."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Chat: Get Incident by ID",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"What's the current status of incident {{incident_id}}?\",\n  \"conversationId\": \"{{conversation_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/chat",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["chat"]
            },
            "description": "Exercises get_incident. `incident_id` comes from the Incidents/Create Incident request — run that first if this incident doesn't exist yet."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Chat: Update Status → IN_PROGRESS",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Move incident {{incident_id}} to IN_PROGRESS. I'm the one working it, changedBy is chat-user@example.com. Note: investigating root cause.\",\n  \"conversationId\": \"{{conversation_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/chat",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["chat"]
            },
            "description": "Exercises update_incident_status: OPEN → IN_PROGRESS."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Chat: Update Status → ON_HOLD",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Put incident {{incident_id}} ON_HOLD — we're waiting on the networking team, changedBy is chat-user@example.com.\",\n  \"conversationId\": \"{{conversation_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/chat",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["chat"]
            },
            "description": "Exercises update_incident_status: IN_PROGRESS → ON_HOLD (feature/MVP addition)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Chat: Resume from ON_HOLD",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"The networking team is done. Resume work on incident {{incident_id}} — move it back to IN_PROGRESS.\",\n  \"conversationId\": \"{{conversation_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/chat",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["chat"]
            },
            "description": "Exercises update_incident_status: ON_HOLD → IN_PROGRESS. Relies on chat memory to know which incident 'it' refers to."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Chat: Resolve Incident",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Mark incident {{incident_id}} as RESOLVED. Note: failover fixed and verified in staging.\",\n  \"conversationId\": \"{{conversation_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/chat",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["chat"]
            },
            "description": "Exercises update_incident_status: IN_PROGRESS → RESOLVED."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Chat: Close Incident",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Close out incident {{incident_id}}, it's been stable for 24 hours.\",\n  \"conversationId\": \"{{conversation_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/chat",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["chat"]
            },
            "description": "Exercises update_incident_status: RESOLVED → CLOSED. Terminal state."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Chat: Get Incident History",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Give me the full timeline of status changes for incident {{incident_id}}, in order.\",\n  \"conversationId\": \"{{conversation_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/chat",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["chat"]
            },
            "description": "Exercises get_incident_history — should reflect every transition made in the requests above (OPEN→IN_PROGRESS→ON_HOLD→IN_PROGRESS→RESOLVED→CLOSED)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Chat: Multi-turn Follow-up",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Reply references prior context', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().reply).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Without me repeating the ID — how many times did that incident's status change, and who made the most recent change?\",\n  \"conversationId\": \"{{conversation_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/chat",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["chat"]
            },
            "description": "No incident ID or tool hint given — this only works if MessageChatMemoryAdvisor is correctly threading conversation_id through so the model recalls the incident and history from the previous turns."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Audit",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Incident History",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response is array', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('Entries have required fields', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.json().forEach(entry => {",
                  "        pm.expect(entry).to.have.all.keys('previousStatus', 'newStatus', 'changedBy', 'changedAt');",
                  "    });",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/{{incident_id}}/history",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["incidents", "{{incident_id}}", "history"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the full chronological audit trail for an incident. Each entry records who changed what status and when, plus optional notes."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "MCP Context",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List MCP Tools",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Returns all 5 registered tools', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.be.an('array').with.lengthOf(5);",
                  "    const names = body.map(t => t.name);",
                  "    ['create_incident', 'get_incident', 'list_incidents', 'update_incident_status', 'get_incident_history']",
                  "        .forEach(n => pm.expect(names).to.include(n));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Each tool has name, description, inputSchema', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.json().forEach(tool => {",
                  "        pm.expect(tool.name).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "        pm.expect(tool.description).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "        pm.expect(tool.inputSchema).to.be.an('object');",
                  "    });",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/mcp/tools",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["mcp", "tools"]
            },
            "description": "Introspects the registered ToolCallbackProvider and returns every MCP tool exposed by this server, with its JSON input schema — useful as a single discovery endpoint for any MCP-aware client."
          }
        }
      ]
